8. The **emitter** rule for integers is not normative — section 1 says only that a reader accepts both forms, so "equal values emit equal text" does not follow from the text. Implementation is correct; the contract is not.
9. `MAX_JSON_TEXT_BYTES` is a magic literal at exactly 4 × `MAX_FRAME_BYTES` (67,108,864). Derive and static-assert it.
10. Hello is the one owner body the bridge decodes and re-encodes (`lib.rs:751`), silently re-canonicalizing it; fuzz lane 1 asserts byte-exact frame round-trip, which holds only if SCB1 decoding is canonical-only. That dependency is unstated.
